            {
              "task": "resume-hooks-silently-lost-7-1",
              "source": "executor",
              "summary": "Every other per-session tmux op carries the same colon blind spot; only ShowEnvironment is now classified.",
              "detail": "wrapSessionTargetErr is wired into ShowEnvironment alone (internal/tmux/tmux.go:590) because that is the one the capture loop classifies against. HasSession (tmux.go:88,97), KillSession (tmux.go:258), SwitchClient (tmux.go:276), SetSessionEnvironment (tmux.go:774), ListClients (internal/tmux/clients.go:19) and SaverPanePIDOrAbsent (internal/tmux/saver_pane_pid.go:13,37) all compose exactTarget and will report a live colon-named session as absent, indistinguishably from a real one. Routing them through the same wrapper is a single mechanical pass, but it changes error classification for callers across cmd, internal/restore and internal/spawn.",
              "files": [
                "internal/tmux/tmux.go",
                "internal/tmux/clients.go",
                "internal/tmux/saver_pane_pid.go",
                "internal/tmux/errors.go"
              ]
            },
            {
              "task": "resume-hooks-silently-lost-7-1",
              "source": "executor",
              "summary": "Two independent definitions of \"a colon may not appear in a session name\" now exist.",
              "detail": "internal/session/naming.go:21 strips : (and .) at generation time via its own strings.NewReplacer, with no reference to the target grammar; tmux.ValidateSessionName (internal/tmux/errors.go) is the new recognition side. They agree today by coincidence, not by construction — the same generation/recognition drift the pane-token work consolidated into internal/nanoid. Deriving the generator sanitiser from the client predicate would close it, but the internal/session to internal/tmux import direction and the . case (a coord separator, not a session one) need deciding first.",
              "files": [
                "internal/session/naming.go",
                "internal/tmux/errors.go"
              ]
